WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.012
Global Config holds shared framework configuration, credential references

00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:06.300
and provider settings.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.112
Choose the intended vault mode and verify its actual runtime support.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.675
Define references for specific targets and purposes.

00:00:15.075 --> 00:00:19.638
A provider selector can write configuration without proving live retrieval.

00:00:20.038 --> 00:00:24.488
Keep the resulting global file, vault material and backups protected.

00:00:25.629 --> 00:00:29.904
Create a clear reference for each target account or password transition.

00:00:30.304 --> 00:00:33.692
The username must match the account requested by the script.

00:00:34.092 --> 00:00:38.142
Use separate references for new local administrators and independent

00:00:38.154 --> 00:00:41.067
nonempty passwords where validation requires them.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.642
A reference name is not a password.

00:00:44.042 --> 00:00:49.029
Validate resolution without printing secret values into logs, tickets

00:00:49.179 --> 00:00:50.654
or tutorial screenshots.

00:00:51.808 --> 00:00:56.808
Config Files is the shared library for saved workflow, script, pipeline

00:00:57.021 --> 00:00:58.133
and recovery inputs.

00:00:58.533 --> 00:01:03.158
Upload or open the intended file, inspect its targets, and save a

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:04.033
descriptive name.

00:01:04.433 --> 00:01:06.521
Retain reviewed versions for recovery.

00:01:06.921 --> 00:01:10.233
Restoring a saved file changes the desired input;

00:01:10.721 --> 00:01:13.883
it does not undo changes already applied on the cluster.

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:19.258
In YAML Studio choose the correct template family and generator.

00:01:19.658 --> 00:01:23.758
Complete the fields, generate the document and inspect validation,

00:01:24.246 --> 00:01:26.421
mapping and adapter-readiness findings.

00:01:26.821 --> 00:01:31.083
Resolve missing references or unsupported properties before saving.

00:01:31.471 --> 00:01:36.108
A successful YAML save is not execution approval, a live connection

00:01:36.108 --> 00:01:37.921
test or a completed deployment.

00:01:38.321 --> 00:01:41.883
Open the corresponding execution workflow for those next steps.

00:01:43.058 --> 00:01:48.246
Before execution, compare the saved YAML, action, target and credential

00:01:48.246 --> 00:01:50.046
references with the approved change.

00:01:50.446 --> 00:01:53.371
Approval can be bound to exact content and filename.

00:01:53.758 --> 00:01:57.096
Editing the document afterward can invalidate that binding.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.433
Never loosen policy to make changed content run.

00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:05.433
Keep sanitized configuration hashes and job identifiers so another

00:02:05.433 --> 00:02:09.083
operator can reconcile what was requested and what actually executed.
